## 2. Confirm access, region, and execution ownership

Obtain the Sauce Labs access approved for your role. Have the authorized integration owner confirm the account, selected data center, devices, and protected credentials.

| Input | What to confirm |
|---|---|
| `SAUCE_USERNAME` | Account identity bound to the approved workflow. |
| `SAUCE_ACCESS_KEY` | Protected access key for that identity. |
| Region | Storage and test execution use the approved compatible data center. |
| Device matrix | Available device names/platform versions, concurrency, and required suites. |
| CLI/custom-step versions | Approved compatible pins and supported inputs/outputs. |

The supplied native-runner example uses `us-west-1`. Current Espresso/XCUITest documentation lists `us-west-1` and `eu-central-1` for these runners. The source's separate US East REST listing must be confirmed for the actual product/API before use. [Espresso configuration](https://docs.saucelabs.com/mobile-apps/automated-testing/espresso-xcuitest/espresso/)

Keep the credential values in the protected platform configuration. A device test needing runtime application configuration or test credentials requires the runner's approved injection mechanism.

