### Supplied `.sauce/config.yml`

This YAML is reproduced exactly from the latest reference. Replace its test-runner marker, class selector, device criteria, and application reference according to the approved configuration.

```yaml
apiVersion: v1alpha
kind: espresso       # or xcuitest for iOS
sauce:
  region: us-west-1
  concurrency: 2

espresso:
  app: storage:$SAUCE_APP_ID
  testApp: storage:<your-test-runner-id>

suites:
  - name: "smoke-tests"
    devices:
      - name: "Google Pixel.*"
        platformVersion: "14"
    testOptions:
      class:
        - com.example.tests.SmokeTestSuite
```

`SAUCE_APP_ID` must resolve to the uploaded application bytes for this run when used in `storage:$SAUCE_APP_ID`. The private registration step also uses the name `SAUCE_APP_ID`. Confirm whether its returned identity is the same storage identity required by the runner before connecting the two.

The separate `testApp` reference must identify the matching instrumentation package. Current vendor documentation defines the distinct application/test inputs and supports `v1alpha`. [Native Android runner fields](https://docs.saucelabs.com/mobile-apps/automated-testing/espresso-xcuitest/espresso/)

